  "questionLabels": [],
  "question": {
    "text": "Consider a circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. If the circle touches the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math>, whose distance from the origin is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math> , then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is equal to _______.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "100",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></math></p><p>The given equation of circle represent centre as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and radius as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math> units.</p><p>Now, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> is tangent to the given circle at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/ae7518bf-d085-4558-a804-b3ee87124b65.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 262px;\"/></p><p>We know that, radius is perpendicular to tangent at the point of tangency.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>⊥</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msqrt><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
